4 #edb/ref 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =4,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415575 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415575 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95362" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415575 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415575 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415575 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "35756e17-7ddb-5db3-9246-f082e3b776e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415575 #edb/ref 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (8-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =8,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{8} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415576 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415576 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95349" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415576 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415576 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415576 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "42bc3fa3-d1ed-5eee-8e63-dbe17bc3a3c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415576 #edb/ref 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0